      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, a standard asphalt shingle roof lasts about 15 to 25 years. High elevation sun, heavy winter snow, and big temperature swings wear out roofs faster here than in milder states. Premium materials like metal or tile last much longer, often 40 to 70+ years.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "15 to 25 years"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan by Roof Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "3-tab asphalt shingles: 12 to 20 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Architectural (dimensional) shingles:\n20 to 30 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Impact-resistant (Class 4) shingles: 30 to 40 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal roofing:\n40 to 70 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Concrete or clay tile: 50 to 100 years"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why Utah Climate Ages Roofs Fast"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Strong UV rays: Utah's high elevation means intense sun. This dries out and cracks asphalt shingle granules quickly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Freeze-thaw cycles:\nSnow melts during the day, flows into tiny cracks, and freezes at night. This ice expands and breaks roofing materials apart."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ice dams: Snow on a warm roof melts, runs to the cold eaves, and freezes. This blocks water and forces it under the shingles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "High winds:\nStrong canyon winds can lift, tear, or loosen edges of shingles."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          10,
          11,
          12
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How to Help Your Roof Last Longer"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check attic airflow: Good vents keep the attic cool. This stops ice dams in winter and heat traps in summer."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Clear off snow and leaves:\nClean your gutters and remove heavy snow buildup when it is safe to do so."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get yearly checks: Have a pro look at your roof after harsh winter storms or high winds."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7,
          8,
          9
        ]
      }
    ],
